\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Benchmark suite and artifact diversity. \textcolor {revisionblue}{\textsc  {AgentDojo}\xspace  and \textsc  {AppWorld}\xspace  contribute 100 fixed sampled case units each; \(\tau ^3\)-bench retail\xspace  contributes all 114 eligible retail base cases; and \textsc  {MiniWoB}\xspace  contributes all 122 eligible cases. Each benchmark is evaluated with three models.} \textsc  {AndroidWorld}\xspace  is a cost-limited mobile-UI stress test with 41 randomly sampled case units and two models. \ensuremath  {\text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}}marks an artifact type that is central to the run evidence; \ensuremath  {\triangle }marks partially retained or benchmark-dependent state. The pool size is the official candidate set used for sampling, not the full advertised benchmark size.}}{6}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:domains}{{1}{6}{Benchmark suite and artifact diversity. \paperupdate {\agentdojo and \appworld contribute 100 fixed sampled case units each; \tauthree contributes all 114 eligible retail base cases; and \miniwob contributes all 122 eligible cases. Each benchmark is evaluated with three models.} \androidworld is a cost-limited mobile-UI stress test with 41 randomly sampled case units and two models. \suiteyes marks an artifact type that is central to the run evidence; \suitepartial marks partially retained or benchmark-dependent state. The pool size is the official candidate set used for sampling, not the full advertised benchmark size}{table.1}{}}
